# Enforce Unix LF line endings for shell scripts
*.sh text eol=lf

# Normalize line endings in the REPOSITORY, not in your working copy.
#
# Without a policy the repo stores a mix (measured 2026-09-20: 52 CRLF blobs
# against 146 LF in a 200-file sample of *.py). That is not cosmetic. A tool
# that rewrites a whole file on Windows flips its endings, and the commit then
# shows every line as changed: a 50-line fix arriving as a 669-line diff,
# unreviewable, with the real change buried. It has happened more than once.
#
# `text=auto` stores LF in the blob and checks out your platform's native
# ending, so Windows working copies stay CRLF and no editor behaviour changes.
# Deliberately NO `eol=lf` here — that would force LF into the working tree.
* text=auto

# Binary — never convert.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
